Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Watching a Qubit: Korotkov's Quantum-Bayesian Formalism for Continuous \
Measurement\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["A weak continuous measurement never collapses a qubit \
outright. It trickles information out through a noisy detector current, and \
the observer folds each noisy reading back into the state with Bayes' rule. \
This essay builds Korotkov's quantum-Bayesian update from primitives and runs \
it: we watch a frozen qubit localize by accumulating likelihood, watch a pure \
state stay exactly pure along a single record while the ensemble dephases, \
drive the qubit with a Rabi field and interleave the measurement as a \
symmetric split, cap the purity with a non-ideal detector, and finally \
recover the closed-form output spectrum from simulated records, where the \
coherent line can never rise more than four times above the detector noise \
floor. A last section closes the loop with the sibling Stratonovich \
stochastic differential equation and exposes the Ito trap that a careless \
integrator falls into.",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: August 18, 2026)", "Text",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: How This Essay Flows", "Section",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["\<\
This essay is a computation-first tour of a single qubit under one symmetric \
broadband detector, in the Markov limit: how a Gaussian likelihood turns a \
noisy current into a state update, why the update is exactly Bayes' rule on \
the populations with the coherence riding along, how a Hamiltonian is \
interleaved with the measurement, what non-ideality costs, and why the \
oscillation line in the output spectrum is bounded by a factor of four. Every \
claim is computed on the spot from base Wolfram Language, so nothing here \
rests on a formula you cannot immediately test and modify.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell["\<\
In other words, I have tried to build a small laboratory for continuous \
measurement of a qubit. I strongly believe in a computation-first narrative \
for learning: in a sense, if I cannot compute it, I cannot claim to \
understand it. The rhythm throughout is concept, then computation, then \
interpretation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["\<\
The environment you see is a live Wolfram notebook. Evaluate the cells from \
top to bottom; the toolkit defined in the next section is used by every \
section that follows, so those dependencies matter. Some cells run \
Monte-Carlo ensembles and take a little while. My suggestion is to focus on \
the output and its meaning first, then unpack the input code. You are not \
locked into any of it: change the rates, the step, the seed, and rerun your \
own experiments.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This essay is the Bayesian-update door into the same physics that the \
sibling essays treat as a stochastic differential equation: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", " ", "vs", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Ito", "/"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " integrates the Stratonovich Bloch-Langevin equation for the state and \
readout, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Manual", " ", "StepLike", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Ito", "/"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 " runs Rouchon trajectories. Section 7 closes the loop by matching that \
Stratonovich equation numerically."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell["\<\
Notation and Conventions: The Detector, the Record, and the Rates\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We work in units where the reduced Planck constant is one, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 ". The qubit is written in the measured (localized) basis ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"1"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"0"},
     "Ket"]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " that the detector couples to, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"1"},
    "Ket"], "=", "{", "1", ",", "0", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"], "=", "{", "0", ",", "1", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 ", so the density matrix is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 " matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " and the single monitored coordinate is the population difference ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 ". A qubit density matrix carries three real numbers, the Bloch vector; the \
detector reads out only the projection ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 ", and the other two ride along in the coherence."
}], "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The detector emits a current whose short-time average over a window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 ". Given a definite state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 " the reading is Gaussian about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 ", and in general it is a linear readout of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 " plus white noise,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], "2"], " ", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
     StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]}], "2"]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 " a white noise of single-sided spectral density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 ". Averaging that current over the window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],
 " leaves a Gaussian of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],
 " about the state-conditioned mean. Two rates organize everything: the \
measurement (information-acquisition) rate and the total ensemble dephasing \
rate,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
      FractionBox[
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
          StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
       RowBox[{"4", 
        StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]]}], ",", 
     "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "\[GreaterEqual]", 
      SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}], ",", 
     "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
         StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "-", 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
         StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}], "\[GreaterEqual]", "0"}]}], ",", 
     "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
         StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
         StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "\[Element]", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}]}]}]}]}], "]"}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 " is any extra dephasing the detector dissipates internally before readout, \
and the ideality ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 " is one exactly for a quantum-limited detector such as a symmetric quantum \
point contact. A symmetric detector has zero output-backaction correlation, \
so there is no unitary phase kick; the back-action is purely informational, \
along the meridians of the Bloch sphere. When a Hamiltonian is present it is \
the symmetric-qubit drive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"q", "b"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
     StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 " with Rabi frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Fix the detector's two output levels and its noise once. We set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"], "=", "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], "=", "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],
 " (so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 ") and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 "; the noise density then follows from whatever measurement rate we choose, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"dI", ",", " ", "i1", ",", " ", "i0", ",", " ", "ic"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dI", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"i1", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"i0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1."}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ic", " ", "=", " ", "0."}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"i1", ",", " ", "i0", ",", " ", "dI"}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the two conditioned means sit symmetrically about zero, so \
a reading's sign is the only hint of which state produced it, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " is the full separation the noise must beat."
}], "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The chance that a state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 " produced a given reading is a Gaussian likelihood; define it as a function \
of the window variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "gaussLike", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
   RowBox[{"mu_", ",", " ", "var_", ",", " ", "ibar_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"ibar", " ", "-", " ", "mu"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "var"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", "var"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell["\<\
This is the single probabilistic object the whole formalism turns on: \
everything downstream is Bayes' rule applied to these two likelihoods.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define the window variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 " and the honest detector draw, sampling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 " from the Gaussian mixture ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], " ", "\|01d4a9", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"], " ", "\|01d4a9", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"], ",", 
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],
 " that the current state predicts:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"avgVar", ",", " ", "drawCurrent"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gm_", ",", " ", "tau_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"dI", "^", "2"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"4", " ", "gm"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "tau"}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"drawCurrent", "[", 
   RowBox[{"rho_", ",", " ", "var_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Clip", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"i1", ",", " ", "i0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", "    ", 
   
   RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "var", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In words, the detector first picks which bell to ring with the current \
populations as weights, then buries the level under Gaussian noise of \
variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 "; the window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 " is the only knob that sharpens it."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell["\<\
Now the heart of the formalism. The exact update over a step, in its cleanest \
form, keeps the populations Bayesian and lets each coherence carry the \
geometric mean of the two likelihoods, with an optional pure-dephasing factor \
for a non-ideal detector:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], " ", "\[LongRightArrow]", " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]], " ", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}]], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"k", "k"}], "TI"]], " ", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], " ", "\[Times]", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], " ", 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"off", "-", 
       RowBox[{"diagonal", "\[NonBreakingSpace]", "only"}]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}],
     FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["gaussLike",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]], ",", 
        StyleBox["D", "TI"], ",", 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell["\<\
Encode that update as one element-wise operation on the matrix:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "bayesUpdate", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
   RowBox[{"rho_", ",", " ", "ibar_", ",", " ", "var_", ",", " ", "gt_"}], 
   "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"p1", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
        RowBox[{"i1", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "ibar"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{"p0", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
        RowBox[{"i0", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "ibar"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
     "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"rho", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"p1", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"p1", " ", "p0"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
            RowBox[{"-", "gt"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"p1", " ", "p0"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
            RowBox[{"-", "gt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "p0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "/",
       "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
          RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "p1"}], " ", "+",
         " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
          RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "p0"}]}], 
       ")"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The diagonal entries pick up ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],
 " and renormalize, which is textbook Gaussian Bayes on the populations; the \
off-diagonal entries pick up ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "0"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 ", so the coherence is pinned to the populations rather than measured \
directly."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Confirm that this update is trace-preserving for any reading, symbolically, \
so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 " stays a density matrix:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"r11", ",", " ", "r10"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "r10", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "r11"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "ibar", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "gt"}], 
        "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "r11", " ", "<", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"var", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ibar", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gt", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell["\<\
As expected, the two updated populations always sum to one: the normalizing \
denominator is exactly the predictive probability of the reading, so \
probability is conserved by construction.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],

Cell["\<\
A single step of the full dynamics interleaves a Hamiltonian half-rotation, \
the Bayesian kick, and another half-rotation, a symmetric (Strang) split that \
is second-order accurate in the step; for a frozen qubit the half-rotation is \
just the identity. Define the step, together with the readouts we will plot:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "measureStep", ",", " ", "blochVec", ",", " ", "purity", ",", " ", 
    "zComp"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"uHalf_", ",", " ", "var_", ",", " ", "gt_"}], "]"}], "[", 
    "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"r1", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"uHalf", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "uHalf", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"uHalf", " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
       RowBox[{"r1", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"drawCurrent", "[", 
         RowBox[{"r1", ",", " ", "var"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", 
        "gt"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "uHalf", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochVec", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "j", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"purity", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
     RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"zComp", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rho", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],

Cell["\<\
That is the entire integrator: a Gaussian draw, an element-wise Bayes kick, \
and two matrix products for the drive. For the output spectrum in Section 6 \
we will also want the record itself, so define a run that emits the stream of \
readings while it measures a driven qubit:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "recordCurrents", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"recordCurrents", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "gm_", ",", " ", "tau_", ",", " ", "gt_", ",", " ", "om_", ",", " ", 
    "nst_", ",", " ", "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"uH", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"om", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"tau", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
          RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
        "r1", ",", " ", "ib"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"r1", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"uH", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "uH", "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ib", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"drawCurrent", "[", 
           RowBox[{"r1", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"uH", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
            RowBox[{"r1", ",", " ", "ib", ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", "gt"}], 
            "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "uH", "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
         "ib"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "nst", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell["\<\
We will return to this record in Section 6; for now it is enough that each \
measurement produces a number, and the state and the record share the very \
same noise.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],

Cell["\<\
1. The Detector's Two Bells: Why One Look Cannot Separate Them\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A weak measurement is weak because a single short look is ambiguous. For a \
state that is definitely ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 " or definitely ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 " the averaged current is a Gaussian centered at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 " with spread ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 "; the two bells overlap heavily until the window ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 " is long enough to pull them apart, and the crossover scale is the \
measurement time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot the two likelihoods ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],
 " against the reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],
 " for windows short, comparable to, and long relative to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"taum", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"dI", "^", "2"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"4", " ", "gm"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"dI", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
             RowBox[{"i1", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
               RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "ibar"}], 
             "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"gaussLike", "[", 
             RowBox[{"i0", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
               RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "ibar"}], 
             "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"ibar", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", "4"}], ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Filling", " ", "->", " ", "Axis"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<averaged current\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<likelihood\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<window \[Tau] = \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
             RowBox[{"tau", "/", "taum"}], "]"}], " ", "<>", 
            " ", "\"\< \[Tau]m\>\""}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "240"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"tau", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"taum", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "6"}], 
            "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Notice that at a quarter of the measurement time the two bells sit almost \
on top of each other, so a single reading barely favors either state; only as \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 " grows past ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 " do the peaks separate and a reading starts to mean something. Information \
is nothing but this shrinking overlap."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell["\<\
2. Populations Follow Bayes: Localization Without a Hamiltonian\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Switch off the Hamiltonian and the record can only report which state we \
are in, never rotate us between them. Start from the equatorial superposition \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"+"},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{"0"},
       "Ket"], "+", 
      TemplateBox[{"1"},
       "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
    SqrtBox["2"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 ", whose two measured-basis populations are equal, and feed each reading \
through the update: the populations move by the likelihood ratio and drift \
toward one pole, a noisy random walk in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 " rather than a jump. The pole that wins is random, with probability equal \
to the initial population, which is the Born rule emerging from accumulated \
evidence."
}], "Text",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run one frozen-qubit trajectory from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 " and watch ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "1000"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"traj", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "17", "]"}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
              RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "]"}],
            ",", "\n", "       ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"zComp", " ", "/@", " ", "traj"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
       "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<z = \[Rho]11 - \[Rho]00\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
       "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<one frozen-qubit record: localization by Bayes\>\""}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell["\<\
The population difference wanders under the noisy evidence and then commits \
to a pole and stays there; the \"collapse\" is the accumulation of \
log-likelihood, not a discontinuous jump.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],

Cell["\<\
3. The Purity Ride-Along: A Pure State Stays Pure in a Single Run\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here is the fact that makes an ideal detector special. The coherence is not \
measured; it rides on the populations through the geometric mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], "0"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],
 ", so the ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "10"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],
 " is left untouched by every update. A state that starts pure therefore \
stays exactly pure along the whole record, never leaving the surface of the \
Bloch sphere, even as its populations localize."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "First confirm the invariance symbolically: check that the ride-along ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "10"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 " is unchanged by an ideal update:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"r11", ",", " ", "r10"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "r10", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "r11"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"u", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "ibar", ",", " ", "var", ",", " ", "0"}], 
        "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"u", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"u", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"u", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"u", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "==",
         " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"r10", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "r10", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"r11", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "r11"}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ",", 
       "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "r11", " ", "<", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"var", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ibar", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ratio is algebraically conserved, so purity is a constant of the ideal \
single-run motion. Watch it hold along a record that starts pure on the \
equator, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 ", while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],
 " localizes:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.02"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "1000"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"traj", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "8", "]"}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
              RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "]"}],
            ",", "\n", "       ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", "traj"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
         "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"zComp", " ", "/@", " ", "traj"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
        "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<value\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<purity Tr[\[Rho]^2]\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<z\>\""}], 
         "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
       "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<ideal detector: purity pinned while z localizes\>\""}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As you may have noticed, the purity sits flat at one while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 " wanders to a pole: information gain alone does not decohere a single run. \
The ensemble decoheres only because different runs localize to different \
poles, which is the subject of Section 7."
}], "Text",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell["\<\
4. Rabi Under Measurement: A Bayes Kick Between Half-Rotations\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now switch on the drive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"q", "b"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
     StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 " and interleave it with the measurement by the symmetric split: a half \
rotation, the Bayesian kick, another half rotation. The measurement pulls the \
state toward the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],
 "-poles while the field rotates it, so a single trajectory is a noisy Rabi \
oscillation whose phase slowly diffuses; a run that starts fully mixed at the \
center of the Bloch ball sharpens into that oscillation as the record accrues."
}], "Text",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run one noisy-Rabi trajectory from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 " and, beside it, a run that starts fully mixed and purifies:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "0.1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.05"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "500"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"om", " ", "=", " ", "1."}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"uH", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"om", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"tau", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"tt", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"pure", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"blochVec", " ", "/@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "5", "]"}], ";", "\n", "       ", 
             RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
                RowBox[{"uH", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], 
                "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"mixed", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"blochVec", " ", "/@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "8", "]"}], ";", "\n", "       ", 
             RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
                RowBox[{"uH", ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], 
                "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", 
             "/@", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "pure", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
            "      ", 
            RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              
              RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<y\>\"", ",", 
               " ", "\"\<z\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              
              RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
               " ", "\"\<Bloch vector\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{
            "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
             " ", "\"\<pure start from |1>: noisy Rabi\>\""}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "250"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
          "     ", 
          RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", 
             "/@", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "mixed", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            
            RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
            "      ", 
            RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              
              RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<y\>\"", ",", 
               " ", "\"\<z\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              
              RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
               " ", "\"\<Bloch vector\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{
            "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
             " ", "\"\<mixed start: purifies into oscillation\>\""}], ",", 
            " ", 
            RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "250"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell["\<\
The pure run oscillates and wobbles but keeps its full Bloch length, while \
the mixed run starts at the origin and swells outward into the same \
phase-locked, slowly diffusing oscillation: the record both drives and \
sharpens the state at once.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell["5. A Non-Ideal Detector: Ideality Caps the Purity", "Section",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A realistic detector loses some of the information it gathers before it \
reaches the output, and that lost information appears as an extra \
pure-dephasing factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 " on the coherence, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],
 ". The measurement keeps localizing at the same informational rate, but the \
coherence is now bled faster than the populations sharpen, so the state \
settles short of the surface at a steady purity set entirely by the ideality ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Overlay the ensemble-averaged purity for a driven qubit measured by \
detectors of ideality ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}], ",", " ", "0.7", ",", " ", "0.4"}]],
   "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 ", the extra dephasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],
 " per step:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "0.1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.05"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "500"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"om", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "80"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"uH", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"om", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"tau", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}], ",", "\n", 
            "      ", 
            RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", 
                RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"1000", " ", "eta"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "k"}],
                    "]"}], ";", "\n", "          ", 
                  RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"uH", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"gm", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"(", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"1", "/", "eta"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], " ",
                     "tau"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
           "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.7", ",", " ", "0.4"}], "}"}]}], 
          "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0.4", ",", " ", "1.02"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<mean purity Tr[\[Rho]^2]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<\[Eta] = 1\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Eta] = 0.7\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<\[Eta] = 0.4\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
       "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
        " ", "\"\<ideality caps the steady purity\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As expected, only the ideal detector holds the state pure; below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 " the purity climbs to a ceiling that drops as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 " drops. The extra dephasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 " is potential information dissipated inside the detector, and only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 " lets you monitor the wavefunction itself."
}], "Text",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell["6. The Output Spectrum and the Factor of Four", "Section",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the payoff. When the drive keeps the qubit oscillating, the Rabi motion \
modulates the very current the detector reports, so the record carries a \
coherent line at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],
 " riding on the white noise floor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],
 ". Korotkov and Averin derived the line in closed form, and its height above \
the floor is bounded: at most four times the noise, reached only for an ideal \
detector, and degrading as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],
 ". This spectrum is not just a calculation: Palacios-Laloy and co-workers \
measured exactly this Rabi line in a continuously monitored superconducting \
qubit, and read its bounded height as a Leggett-Garg (temporal Bell) test of \
macroscopic realism (Nature Physics 6, 442 (2010), arXiv:1005.3435)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["I", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "+", "4", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
       StyleBox["R", "TI"], "2"], " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
         SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
          StyleBox["R", "TI"], "2"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "+", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"]}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
        StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Half of that four is the ordinary spectrum of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],
 "; the other half is a purely nonclassical correlation between the detector \
noise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 " and the back-action it exerts on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],
 ", which no classical harmonic signal can produce. The record we simulate \
carries both halves automatically, because the same reading that enters the \
spectrum also drives the Bayesian kick."
}], "Text",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Simulate long records in the good-oscillation regime ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "\[GreaterGreater]", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],
 ", average the periodogram over an ensemble for three idealities, and \
overlay the closed form (dashed):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "0.05"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"om", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.05"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "14000"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "200"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"etas", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "0.25"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "gd", ",", " ", "sClosed", ",", " ", "spec", ",", " ", "specs"}], "}"}],
      ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gd", "[", "eta_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gm", "/", "eta"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"sClosed", "[", 
        RowBox[{"eta_", ",", " ", "w_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", "eta", " ", 
         RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"gd", "[", "eta", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
               RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"gd", "[", "eta", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"spec", "[", "recs_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
             RowBox[{"recs", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "half", ",", 
           " ", "ws", ",", " ", "p", ",", " ", "fl"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
         "    ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"half", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Quotient", "[", 
            RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ws", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"2.", " ", "Pi", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"s", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "/", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"n", " ", "tau"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "half"}], "}"}]}], 
            "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], 
                ")"}], "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", ";;", " ", "half"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
              "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "recs"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"fl", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Median", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Pick", "[", 
             RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"UnitStep", "[", 
               RowBox[{"ws", " ", "-", " ", "2.5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "1"}], 
             "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"ws", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"2", " ", ";;", " ", 
                RowBox[{"-", "2"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"MovingAverage", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"p", "/", "fl"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
           "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"LaunchKernels", "[", "]"}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"DistributeDefinitions", "[", "\"\<Global`\>\"", "]"}], ";", 
      "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"specs", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"spec", "[", 
          RowBox[{"ParallelTable", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"recordCurrents", "[", 
             RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"gd", "[", "eta", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "gm"}], 
                ")"}], " ", "tau"}], ",", " ", "om", ",", " ", "nst", ",", 
              " ", 
              RowBox[{"7000", " ", "+", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
                RowBox[{"1000", " ", "eta"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "k"}]}], 
             "]"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", "etas"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
      "  ", 
      RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
         RowBox[{"specs", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "2.2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
          "    ", 
          RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<angular frequency \[Omega]\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<spectral density / noise floor\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
          "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<simulated \[Eta] = 1\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<simulated \[Eta] = 0.5\>\"", ",", 
             " ", "\"\<simulated \[Eta] = 0.25\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
          "    ", 
          RowBox[{
          "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
           " ", "\"\<output spectrum: the coherent line and the factor of \
four\>\""}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"w", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"sClosed", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", "w"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
               "w", ",", " ", "0.2", ",", " ", "2.2", ",", " ", "0.002"}], 
               "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"eta", ",", " ", "etas"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
          "    ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Thick", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], 
            "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each simulated line sits on the closed-form Lorentzian, and the coherent \
peak climbs toward four times the floor for the ideal detector and falls off \
as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],
 ": the line is bounded because half of its area is the noise-backaction \
correlation, which saturates only when every bit of dephasing is \
informational."
}], "Text",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],

Cell["7. Cross-Check: The Stratonovich SDE and the Ito Trap", "Section",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same physics is a Bloch-Langevin stochastic differential equation in \
the sibling essay ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", " ", "vs", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Ito", "/"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],
 ". The Bayesian update and that Stratonovich equation must agree as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 ", and comparing them exposes the classic Ito trap. The ensemble coherence \
decays at the total rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],
 "; in the Ito form of the coherence equation that decay is the term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", "4", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],
 ", which is not physical decoherence at all but the Stratonovich-to-Ito \
drift correction. Hand the Stratonovich right-hand side to a plain Ito-Euler \
stepper without that term and the coherence decays at the wrong rate."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Overlay the ensemble coherence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],
 " from three routes started on the equator: the Bayesian update, the correct \
Ito stepper with the drift term, and the naive stepper missing it, against \
the exact decay ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 " (dashed):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "300"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ntr", " ", "=", " ", "1500"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "bayes", ",", 
       " ", "ito", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"tt", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}], " ", "tau"}]}], ",", " ", 
       "run"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"bayes", "[", "rho_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"measureStep", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", 
          "0."}], "]"}], "[", "rho", "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ito", "[", "drift_", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"x_", ",", " ", "z_"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"xb", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
            RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "v", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
         "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"x", " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"z", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm"}], ")"}], " ", "x", " ", "xb", " ", 
             "tau"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"drift", " ", "gm", " ", "x", " ", "tau"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"z", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
               RowBox[{"z", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"2", " ", "gm"}], ")"}], " ", "xb", " ", "tau"}]}]}], 
          "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"run", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "stepper_", ",", " ", "init_", ",", " ", "read_", ",", " ", "seed_"}],
         "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"read", " ", "/@", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
              RowBox[{"seed", " ", "+", " ", "k"}], "]"}], ";", " ", 
             RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
              RowBox[{"stepper", ",", " ", "init", ",", " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}],
             "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntr"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n",
       "  ", 
      RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"run", "[", 
              RowBox[{"bayes", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
               
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"2", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
                   RowBox[{"#", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], " ", 
                 "&"}], ")"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
          "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"run", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"ito", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", "First", ",",
                " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"run", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"ito", "[", "0", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", "First", ",",
                " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        
        RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.02"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        
        RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<time (units of 1/\[CapitalGamma]m)\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<ensemble coherence \[LeftAngleBracket]x\
\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<Bayesian update\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<Ito with +(\[CapitalDelta]I)^2/4S drift\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<naive Ito, drift dropped\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
        "   ", 
        RowBox[{
        "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
         " ", "\"\<the Ito trap: the drift correction IS the dephasing\>\""}],
         ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"Black", ",", " ", "Dashed", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"-", "gm"}], " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], 
            "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This confirms that the Bayesian update and the correct Ito stepper both \
fall onto the exact ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],
 " curve, while the naive stepper never dephases at all: the missing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", "4", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],
 " term was the entire ensemble decoherence. The Bayesian form has no \
calculus ambiguity to begin with, because it is discrete Gaussian Bayes \
between unitary half-steps; the stochastic differential equation reproduces \
it only when the Stratonovich-to-Ito drift is kept."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell["\<\
8. The Other Back-Action: The Phase Kick and the Second Quadrature\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every detector in this essay has been symmetric: a quantum point contact \
whose two output levels carry the same noise, so the correlation between the \
detector's output noise and the disturbance it feeds back to the qubit \
vanishes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 ". That is exactly why the back-action has been purely informational. Each \
reading squeezes the populations and slides the state along a meridian of the \
Bloch sphere, changing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 ", and nothing turns the coherence. A general detector is not so gentle: \
alongside the informational disturbance it applies a second, physical one, an \
active rotation of the coherence about the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],
 "-axis, driven by the very same record."
}], "Text",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, there are two back-actions, and so far we have felt only \
one. Korotkov names them \"spooky\" and \"realistic\". The spooky \
(informational) back-action is the non-unitary Bayes factor we have used \
throughout: it carries no physical mechanism, it is pure information, and it \
moves the state along meridians, changing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],
 ". The realistic (phase) back-action is unitary: it is a genuine rotation of \
the coherence about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],
 ", along the parallels of constant latitude, and it needs a physical \
mechanism, such as the fluctuating level shift an asymmetric detector \
imprints on the qubit. For a symmetric detector the second one is switched \
off; for a general one it is not."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Concretely, the coherence picks up one extra factor. Where the ideal update \
multiplied ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "10"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 " by the geometric mean of the two likelihoods, a general detector \
multiplies it also by a record-driven phase,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->300048012,ExpressionUUID->"106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "10"], " ", "\[LongRightArrow]", " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "10"], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "0"]}]], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"k", "k"}], "TI"]], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", " ", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "a rotation of the coherence through an angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],
 " set by the correlation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["K", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],
 " and the integrated current ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],
 " of that step. In circuit QED this second channel is not abstract: a \
phase-preserving amplifier reports two output quadratures at once, and while \
the in-phase quadrature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],
 " carries the informational back-action, the second quadrature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],
 " is the one that carries the phase kick."
}], "Text",
 CellID->588230824,ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because the phase kick is unitary, it never touches a single run's purity: \
the ride-along of Section 3 still holds exactly, and a pure state stays on \
the surface of the Bloch sphere. It shows up instead in the ensemble, because \
different records wind the coherence by different angles and the average of \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 " shrinks toward zero. The total ensemble dephasing rate therefore splits \
into three pieces,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2099309037,ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", "=", 
    UnderscriptBox[
     UnderscriptBox[
      FractionBox[
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
          StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
       RowBox[{"4", 
        StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], "\[UnderBrace]"], 
     StyleBox["informational",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox[
     UnderscriptBox[
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["K", "TI"], "2"], 
        StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], "4"], "\[UnderBrace]"], 
     StyleBox["phase",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox[
     UnderscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[UnderBrace]"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"extra", "\[NonBreakingSpace]", "environment"}],
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->512383039,ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and the fraction of that rate which is informational is precisely the \
number that fixes the height of the Section 6 line: peak-to-pedestal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"=", 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "\[CapitalGamma]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 ". In Section 6 the peak degraded as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],
 " only because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],
 " made ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],
 "; in general the height is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],
 ", and the phase back-action pushes it down even when the detector wastes no \
information internally (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 "). A phase-preserving amplifier splits its dephasing evenly between the two \
quadratures, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"], "\[LessEqual]", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 " and its coherent line can rise at most twice above the noise floor, never \
four times."
}], "Text",
 CellID->273308241,ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All of this is one statement about the measurement operator. The general \
weak-measurement (Kraus) operator for a reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],
 " factorizes into a unitary times a positive part,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1809098798,ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], 
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "\[Dagger]"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]}]]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], " ", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "/", "2"}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "\[Dagger]"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SqrtBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"]], 
      TemplateBox[{"1"},
       "Ket"], 
      TemplateBox[{"1"},
       "Bra"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SqrtBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "0"]], 
      TemplateBox[{"0"},
       "Ket"], 
      RowBox[{
       TemplateBox[{"0"},
        "Bra"], "."}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->156430199,ExpressionUUID->"4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The positive square-root factor is exactly the informational Bayes update \
we built in Section 2; the unitary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],
 " is the phase rotation, which we quietly set to the identity by taking ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],
 ". Everything in this essay so far has been the special case ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "=", "\|01d7d9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->724760089,ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Turn the phase kick on and watch it act. Run one record through both \
detectors from the same pure equatorial start ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{"+"},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],
 ", and plot the coherence in the equatorial ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],
 " plane for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[NotEqual]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 " beside the symmetric ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 " run:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->168408080,ExpressionUUID->"640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gm", " ", "=", " ", "0.3"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tau", " ", "=", " ", "0.05"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nst", " ", "=", " ", "80"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"kk", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"seed", " ", "=", " ", "3"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"avgVar", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gm", ",", " ", "tau"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"plus", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"phaseStep", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", "kval", "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
            RowBox[{"rho", ",", "\n", "      ", 
             RowBox[{"With", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"ib", " ", "=", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"drawCurrent", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
               "       ", 
               RowBox[{"With", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"uk", " ", "=", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "kval", " ", "ib", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"tau", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"I", " ", "kval", " ", "ib", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"tau", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
                  "}"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
                 RowBox[{"uk", " ", ".", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"bayesUpdate", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                   "rho", ",", " ", "ib", ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", "0."}], 
                   "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "uk", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}],
               "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"pathK", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"#", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"#", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "@*",
                " ", "blochVec"}], ")"}], " ", "/@", "\n", "        ", 
             RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", " ", 
               RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"phaseStep", "[", "kk", "]"}], ",", " ", "plus", ",",
                  " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"path0", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"#", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"#", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "@*",
                " ", "blochVec"}], ")"}], " ", "/@", "\n", "        ", 
             RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", " ", 
               RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"phaseStep", "[", "0.", "]"}], ",", " ", "plus", ",",
                  " ", "nst"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
         "    ", 
         RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"pathK", ",", " ", "path0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",",
            " ", 
           RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"\"\<Bloch x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Bloch y\>\""}], 
             "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             
             RowBox[{"\"\<K \[NotEqual] 0: phase + informational\>\"", ",", 
              " ", "\"\<K = 0: informational only\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
           "     ", 
           RowBox[{
           "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
            " ", "\"\<same record: the phase back-action winds the coherence \
about z\>\""}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
           RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"GrayLevel", "[", "0.6", "]"}], ",", " ", "Dashed", ",",
               " ", 
              RowBox[{"Circle", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "1"}], 
               "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->811283638,ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same record that localizes the populations now also carries the \
coherence around the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],
 "-axis: the symmetric detector slides the state straight inward along a \
meridian with the phase pinned (the radial ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],
 " track), while the general detector adds the parallel motion, a unitary \
turn through an angle equal to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["K", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 " times the integrated current (the winding ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[NotEqual]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 " track), so every single run stays exactly as pure as before even though \
the ensemble of records now dephases faster. Turning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],
 " fully on, and letting two such detectors act at once, is where the sibling \
essay ",
 Cell["Watching-Two-Axes.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],
 " picks up."
}], "Text",
 CellID->207978548,ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us (and What Comes Next)", "Section",
 CellID->437474228,ExpressionUUID->"74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],

Cell["\<\
You now have a complete, computation-first toolkit for one qubit under one \
symmetric broadband detector: a Gaussian likelihood, a Bayes kick on the \
populations with the coherence riding along, a symmetric split that adds a \
Hamiltonian, a pure-dephasing factor for non-ideality, an ensemble of records \
whose spectrum recovers the Korotkov-Averin line and its factor-of-four \
bound, and a first look at the phase back-action a general detector adds on \
top of all this. Before moving on, the points that were computed and verified \
along the way:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->874582697,ExpressionUUID->"735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The detector separates the two states only gradually; information is the \
shrinking overlap of two Gaussians, on the scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->11631581,ExpressionUUID->"3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],

Cell["\<\
With no Hamiltonian the populations follow Gaussian Bayes and localize to a \
pole with the initial-population probability, the Born rule as accumulated \
evidence.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1933762060,ExpressionUUID->"045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ideal detector conserves ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "10"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "00"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],
 " exactly, so a pure state stays pure along a single record; the ensemble \
dephases only because runs localize to different poles."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1055776787,ExpressionUUID->"33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],

Cell["\<\
A symmetric split interleaves the Rabi drive with the Bayes kick, turning a \
mixed state into a phase-locked, slowly diffusing oscillation.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1859711813,ExpressionUUID->"794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Non-ideality is a pure-dephasing factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],
 "; the steady purity is capped by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],
 ", and only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],
 " monitors the wavefunction."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1348896709,ExpressionUUID->"57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The output spectrum carries a coherent line at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],
 " whose height above the floor is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],
 ", at most four, half of it the nonclassical noise-backaction correlation."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1427211115,ExpressionUUID->"10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Bayesian update and the Stratonovich SDE agree as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],
 "; a naive Ito stepper that drops the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", "4", 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],
 " drift loses the entire ensemble dephasing."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2099805207,ExpressionUUID->"0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A general (non-symmetric) detector adds a unitary, record-driven phase kick \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],
 " to the coherence; it keeps every single run pure yet adds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],
 " to the dephasing, so the coherent line is really ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "~"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],
 ", at most twice the floor for a phase-preserving amplifier, and the whole \
measurement reads ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["I", "TI"], "_"]]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1402006442,ExpressionUUID->"25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The natural continuations are the pieces this essay deliberately left out: \
a finite detector bandwidth where the qubit and the cavity field must be \
tracked together, measurement feedback to lock the oscillation, two detectors \
reading non-commuting observables at once, and two-qubit measurement-induced \
entanglement. The finite-bandwidth and feedback pieces are still doors to \
open; the last two are now companion essays in their own right, ",
 Cell["Watching-Two-Axes.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],
 " (two non-commuting axes) and ",
 Cell["Watching-Two-Qubits.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],
 " (a shared parity meter). Each is a small extension of the same update."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1901179466,ExpressionUUID->"7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (February 17, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"
]
